<title>JAPAN: Taisei bid only on share buy-back plan.</title>
<headline>Taisei bid only on share buy-back plan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Taisei Corp, a major general contractor, were bid-only on Monday morning, cheered by the firm's announcement on Friday that it would buy back up to 25 billion yen worth, or 55 million, of its shares, traders said.</p>
<p>The share priced was quoted bid-only at 451 yen as of 0049 GMT, above Friday's close of 431 yen.  </p>
<p>&quot;Uncertainties in the overall construction industry have not eased yet, but the share buy-back will help the share price firm,&quot; said a trader at a medium-sized securities house.</p>
</text>
